IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc4-sch6-descriptors`
IMPORT `uc4-sch7-descriptors`
IMPORT `uc4-sch8-sch9-treated`
IMPORT `uc4-part5-capability`

-- Tests of uc4-part5-capability.l4: regulations 38, 39, 40 and 40A.
-- Expected values are written by hand from the text, beside the assertion.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Fixtures: Schedule 8 and 9 circumstances (nothing applies, or one paragraph).
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sch 8 circumstances`
`test — Schedule 8 with paragraph 1 set` a MEANS `Sch 8 circumstances` WITH
    `paragraph 1 facts` IS `Sch 8 para 1 treatment facts` WITH
        `receiving regular weekly treatment by way of haemodialysis for chronic renal failure` IS a
        `receiving treatment by way of plasmapheresis` IS FALSE
        `receiving regular weekly treatment by way of total parenteral nutrition for gross impairment of enteric function` IS FALSE
        `recovering from any of those forms of treatment` IS FALSE
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work` IS FALSE
    `paragraph 2 facts` IS `Sch 8 para 2 hospital facts` WITH
        `undergoing medical or other treatment as a patient in a hospital or similar institution` IS FALSE
        `attending a residential programme of rehabilitation for the treatment of drug or alcohol dependency` IS FALSE
        `has been advised to stay for a period of 24 hours or longer following medical or other treatment` IS FALSE
        adviser IS Practitioner WITH
            `registered medical practitioner` IS FALSE
            `registered nurse` IS FALSE
            `occupational therapist or physiotherapist` IS FALSE
            `registered with a regulatory body established under section 60 of the Health Act 1999` IS FALSE
        `recovering from such treatment` IS FALSE
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work` IS FALSE
    `paragraph 3 facts` IS `Sch 8 para 3 facts` WITH
        `nation in which the claimant is` IS England
        `excluded or abstains from work pursuant to a request or notice in writing lawfully made or given under an enactment` IS FALSE
        `otherwise prevented from working pursuant to an enactment` IS FALSE
        `it is known or reasonably suspected that the claimant is infected or contaminated, or has been in contact with a case` IS FALSE
        `incidence or spread of infection or contamination within section 45A(3) of the Public Health (Control of Disease) Act 1984 for which regulations are made under Part 2A of that Act` IS FALSE
        `tuberculosis or an infectious disease to which regulation 9 of the Public Health (Aircraft) Regulations 1979 or regulation 10 of the Public Health (Ships) Regulations 1979 applies` IS FALSE
        `infectious disease within section 1(5) of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008, or exposure to an organism causing that disease` IS FALSE
        `contamination within section 1(5) of that Act, or exposure to a contaminant` IS FALSE
        `sections 56 to 58 of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008 (compensation) apply to it` IS FALSE
    `paragraph 4 facts` IS `Sch 8 para 4 risk facts` WITH
        `suffering from a specific illness, disease or disablement` IS FALSE
        `by reason of it there would be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person were the claimant found not to have limited capability for work` IS FALSE
        `the risk could be reduced by a significant amount by reasonable adjustments being made in the claimant's workplace` IS FALSE
        `the risk could be reduced by a significant amount by the claimant taking medication prescribed by a registered medical practitioner treating the claimant` IS FALSE
    `paragraph 5 facts` IS `Sch 8 para 5 disease facts` WITH
        `suffering from a life threatening disease` IS FALSE
        `there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrollable by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS FALSE
        `there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrolled by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS FALSE
        `there is a reasonable cause for the disease not to be controlled by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS FALSE
    `paragraph 6 facts` IS `Sch 8 para 6 facts` WITH
        `reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS FALSE
        `entitled to` IS EMPTY

GIVEN risk IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sch 8 circumstances`
`test — Schedule 8 with paragraph 4 set` risk MEANS `Sch 8 circumstances` WITH
    `paragraph 1 facts` IS `Sch 8 para 1 treatment facts` WITH
        `receiving regular weekly treatment by way of haemodialysis for chronic renal failure` IS FALSE
        `receiving treatment by way of plasmapheresis` IS FALSE
        `receiving regular weekly treatment by way of total parenteral nutrition for gross impairment of enteric function` IS FALSE
        `recovering from any of those forms of treatment` IS FALSE
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work` IS FALSE
    `paragraph 2 facts` IS `Sch 8 para 2 hospital facts` WITH
        `undergoing medical or other treatment as a patient in a hospital or similar institution` IS FALSE
        `attending a residential programme of rehabilitation for the treatment of drug or alcohol dependency` IS FALSE
        `has been advised to stay for a period of 24 hours or longer following medical or other treatment` IS FALSE
        adviser IS Practitioner WITH
            `registered medical practitioner` IS FALSE
            `registered nurse` IS FALSE
            `occupational therapist or physiotherapist` IS FALSE
            `registered with a regulatory body established under section 60 of the Health Act 1999` IS FALSE
        `recovering from such treatment` IS FALSE
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work` IS FALSE
    `paragraph 3 facts` IS `Sch 8 para 3 facts` WITH
        `nation in which the claimant is` IS England
        `excluded or abstains from work pursuant to a request or notice in writing lawfully made or given under an enactment` IS FALSE
        `otherwise prevented from working pursuant to an enactment` IS FALSE
        `it is known or reasonably suspected that the claimant is infected or contaminated, or has been in contact with a case` IS FALSE
        `incidence or spread of infection or contamination within section 45A(3) of the Public Health (Control of Disease) Act 1984 for which regulations are made under Part 2A of that Act` IS FALSE
        `tuberculosis or an infectious disease to which regulation 9 of the Public Health (Aircraft) Regulations 1979 or regulation 10 of the Public Health (Ships) Regulations 1979 applies` IS FALSE
        `infectious disease within section 1(5) of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008, or exposure to an organism causing that disease` IS FALSE
        `contamination within section 1(5) of that Act, or exposure to a contaminant` IS FALSE
        `sections 56 to 58 of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008 (compensation) apply to it` IS FALSE
    `paragraph 4 facts` IS `Sch 8 para 4 risk facts` WITH
        `suffering from a specific illness, disease or disablement` IS risk
        `by reason of it there would be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person were the claimant found not to have limited capability for work` IS risk
        `the risk could be reduced by a significant amount by reasonable adjustments being made in the claimant's workplace` IS FALSE
        `the risk could be reduced by a significant amount by the claimant taking medication prescribed by a registered medical practitioner treating the claimant` IS FALSE
    `paragraph 5 facts` IS `Sch 8 para 5 disease facts` WITH
        `suffering from a life threatening disease` IS FALSE
        `there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrollable by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS FALSE
        `there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrolled by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS FALSE
        `there is a reasonable cause for the disease not to be controlled by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS FALSE
    `paragraph 6 facts` IS `Sch 8 para 6 facts` WITH
        `reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS FALSE
        `entitled to` IS EMPTY

`test — no Schedule 8 circumstance` MEANS `test — Schedule 8 with paragraph 1 set` FALSE
`test — Schedule 8 paragraph 1 applies` MEANS `test — Schedule 8 with paragraph 1 set` TRUE
`test — Schedule 8 paragraph 4 applies` MEANS `test — Schedule 8 with paragraph 4 set` TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 38: the record the other pieces read.
#ASSERT (`reg 38 — what Part 5 decides about a claimant` TRUE FALSE TRUE)'s `limited capability for work`
#ASSERT NOT ((`reg 38 — what Part 5 decides about a claimant` TRUE FALSE TRUE)'s `limited capability for work and work-related activity`)
#ASSERT (`reg 38 — what Part 5 decides about a claimant` TRUE FALSE TRUE)'s `severe conditions criteria claimant`
#ASSERT (`reg 38 — what Part 5 decides about a claimant` FALSE TRUE FALSE)'s `limited capability for work and work-related activity`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 39(1): determined under this Part, or under Part 4 of the ESA Regulations, or treated (paragraph (6), Schedule 8).
#ASSERT `reg 39(1) — limited capability for work` TRUE FALSE `test — no Schedule 8 circumstance`
#ASSERT `reg 39(1) — limited capability for work` FALSE TRUE `test — no Schedule 8 circumstance`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 39(1) — limited capability for work` FALSE FALSE `test — no Schedule 8 circumstance`)
-- Treated by Schedule 8 paragraph 1.
#ASSERT `reg 39(1) — limited capability for work` FALSE FALSE `test — Schedule 8 paragraph 1 applies`
-- Treated by paragraph 4: allowed where the claimant has not been found to have the status by an assessment under this Part.
#ASSERT `reg 39(1) — limited capability for work` FALSE FALSE `test — Schedule 8 paragraph 4 applies`
-- Found by an assessment under this Part: limited capability for work either way.
#ASSERT `reg 39(1) — limited capability for work` TRUE FALSE `test — Schedule 8 paragraph 4 applies`

-- Regulation 39(2): a claimant can be assessed under this Part only if they have some specific disease or bodily or mental disablement.
#ASSERT `reg 39(2) — a claimant can be assessed under this Part` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 39(2) — a claimant can be assessed under this Part` FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 39(3): 15 points, from Part 1, from Part 2, or by a combination of the Parts.
#ASSERT `reg 39(3) — the number of points that gives limited capability for work` EQUALS 15
